easuring"},{"text":"Assembly"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to understand:"},{"type":"p","text":"How digital geometry eventually becomes a physical object."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Digital Modeling & Fabrication Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Start building a digital-to-physical workflow."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Modeling"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"SketchUp"},{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"Basic 3D modeling"},{"text":"NURBS fundamentals"},{"text":"Mesh modeling"},{"text":"Surface modeling"},{"text":"Solid modeling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Fabrication"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Laser cutting"},{"text":"CNC routing"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"2D cutting"},{"text":"Milling"},{"text":"Drilling"},{"text":"Assembly"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Kerf"},{"text":"Tolerances"},{"text":"Toolpaths"},{"text":"Material thickness"},{"text":"Machine limitations"},{"text":"Joint design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Computational Design"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the key transition from conventional architecture to algorithmic design."},{"type":"h","text":"Rhino + Grasshopper"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parametric modeling"},{"text":"Generative geometry"},{"text":"Curves"},{"text":"Surfaces"},{"text":"Meshes"},{"text":"Data trees"},{"text":"Lists"},{"text":"Transformations"},{"text":"Attractors"},{"text":"Pattern generation"},{"text":"Optimization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Parameters","Algorithm","Geometry","Design Variations","Fabrication"]},{"type":"h","text":"Computational Geometry"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parametric surfaces"},{"text":"Panelization"},{"text":"Tessellation"},{"text":"Voronoi patterns"},{"text":"Mesh subdivision"},{"text":"Folding"},{"text":"Contouring"},{"text":"Lofting"},{"text":"Morphing"},{"text":"Structural geometry"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of manually designing 500 panels:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design Rules","Grasshopper Definition","500 Unique Panels","Panel Data","Fabrication Files"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is the foundation of computational fabrication."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Digital Manufacturing"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how design files become machine instructions."},{"type":"h","text":"CNC"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Toolpaths"},{"text":"Milling"},{"text":"Cutting depth"},{"text":"Tool selection"},{"text":"Feed rate"},{"text":"Material constraints"},{"text":"Nesting"},{"text":"CNC file preparation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Laser Cutting"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Kerf"},{"text":"Cutting"},{"text":"Engraving"},{"text":"Layer organization"},{"text":"Material thickness"},{"text":"Assembly logic"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D Printing"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FDM"},{"text":"Resin printing"},{"text":"Large-format printing concepts"},{"text":"Slicing"},{"text":"Supports"},{"text":"Layer height"},{"text":"Infill"},{"text":"Print orientation"},{"text":"Material behavior"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Advanced Digital Fabrication"},{"type":"p","text":"Now combine computational design with real fabrication systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Robotic Fabrication"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Robotic arms"},{"text":"Robotic milling"},{"text":"Robotic cutting"},{"text":"Robotic 3D printing"},{"text":"Robotic assembly"},{"text":"Multi-axis fabrication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Parametric Model","Toolpath Generation","Robot Simulation","Collision Checking","Machine Code","Robot","Physical Object"]},{"type":"h","text":"Robotic Simulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore to